  "content": {
    "id": "p26-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "$f(x)=2x-3$, $g(x)=\\sqrt{x}$, $h(x)=x^2+1$.\n\nSimplify these expressions, hence state the domain.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p26-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$f(g(x))$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2\\sqrt{x}-3$, domain $[0,\\infty)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(g(x))&=f(\\sqrt{x})\\\\f(g(x))&=2\\sqrt{x}-3\\end{align*}$$\nThe square root requires $x\\geq 0$. Domain: $[0,\\infty)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$g(f(x))$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sqrt{2x-3}$, domain $[\\tfrac32,\\infty)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}g(f(x))&=g(2x-3)\\\\g(f(x))&=\\sqrt{2x-3}\\end{aligned}$$\nThe square root requires:\n$$\\begin{aligned}2x-3&\\geq 0\\\\x&\\geq\\frac32\\end{aligned}$$\nDomain: $[\\tfrac32,\\infty)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q4-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$h(f(x))$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$4x^2-12x+10$, domain $\\mathbb{R}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}h(f(x))&=(2x-3)^2+1\\\\h(f(x))&=4x^2-12x+9+1\\\\h(f(x))&=4x^2-12x+10\\end{align*}$$\nBoth functions are defined for every real input. Domain: $\\mathbb{R}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q4-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$g(h(x))$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sqrt{x^2+1}$, domain $\\mathbb{R}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}g(h(x))&=g(x^2+1)\\\\g(h(x))&=\\sqrt{x^2+1}\\end{align*}$$\nSince $x^2+1\\geq 1$ for every real $x$, the square root is always defined. Domain: $\\mathbb{R}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      }
    ]
  },
